1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,025
A replay of one real delivery on the Kiro Crew board: six AI roles in the five AI-DLC phases. The agents' notes are in Chinese.

2
00:00:09,075 --> 00:00:15,437
Triage gate: a person decides each finding, and every option cites the interface specification.

3
00:00:15,488 --> 00:00:24,042
Who did what, built from the audit trail: people appear only at the gates and on the bench.

4
00:00:24,092 --> 00:00:29,134
Tests first: the tester's seven new tests fail on the old code.

5
00:00:29,184 --> 00:00:33,434
The checks before the bench send each failure back to the role that owns it.

6
00:00:33,484 --> 00:00:40,434
Fix rounds: the agents change the code, and the checks keep sending it back until it passes.

7
00:00:40,484 --> 00:00:46,767
When a role can no longer fix what failed, the run stops and hands over to a person.

8
00:00:46,817 --> 00:00:56,149
The reviewer reads only the changes. Its open point also goes to a person to decide.

9
00:00:56,199 --> 00:01:02,369
On the bench, a person approves the deploy and then the replay. Both post-bench checks pass.

10
00:01:02,419 --> 00:01:09,045
The first independent rerun failed on an app defect, fixed since. The owner resumed it, and it passed.

11
00:01:09,095 --> 00:01:16,712
All seven checks pass on the rerun, and the release owner signs off on the evidence page, at the emulation tier.

12
00:01:16,762 --> 00:01:24,628
The scorecard holds only measured numbers. Its top row adds two runs; the per-run row is this delivery.
